id: records/articulation-floor
title: "the measured floor"
kind: floor
record_shape: header
status: active
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-13; computed by lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs computeFloor over the closed answer records; there are none yet, so every count is zero and nothing is invented"
updated: 2026-09-13
loop_ref: core/articulation-floor.yawn
template_ref: templates/floor.yawn
public_slice: https://yawn.bot/status

purpose: >
  The global floor the public slice reads, plus one row per axis that has been
  sealed. It is recomputed from the answer ledger each pulse; where that ledger
  persists is an open question (questions/open-questions.yawn), so until it is
  answered the closed answers live on the principal's device and this record
  shows n zero honestly. A runtime may compute a device-local floor beside it
  and must label it as such.

axis: all
n: 0
blind_n: 0
anchored_n: 0
answer_accuracy: 0
reason_accuracy: 0
curve: []
last_break: null
t_computed: null

axes:
  rule: "one row per axis with at least one seal; n counts closed answers on this device-independent record only"
  rows:
    - axis: floor
      source: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
      sealed: 1
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
    - axis: exclusivity
      source: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
      sealed: 1
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
    - axis: reversibility
      source: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
      sealed: 1
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
    - axis: timing
      source: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
      sealed: 1
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
    - axis: fidelity
      source: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
      sealed: 1
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
    - axis: locus
      source: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
      sealed: 1
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
    - axis: levels
      source: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
      sealed: 1
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
    - axis: decisions
      source: records/yawn.bot-state.yawn
      sealed: 12
      n: 0
      reason_accuracy: 0
      note: "the twelve queued decisions, one seal each, anchored: the recommendation is shown beside the candidates"

readout:
  verdict: no-data
  note: "No closed record yet. The floor cannot be backfilled; it starts when the first sealed question is answered and its reason checked."
  rule: core/articulation-floor.yawn#readout

boundary:
  - "n zero is shown as n zero; a floor below ten closed records is reported, never read as a verdict"
  - "a device-local floor a runtime computes beside this record is that device's, not this record's"
  - "this record measures the representation; it is never a claim about the person"

proof:
  covers:
    - axis
    - n
    - readout
  condition: >
    Every axis row names a record whose seals scripts/validate-articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs
    verifies; the counts are zero until an answer ledger exists that
    lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs computeFloor can read.
  source:
    - question-packets/polanyi.yawn
    - records/yawn.bot-state.yawn
    - lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs
  status: contract-defined
